# Auth

Users, sign-in and access tokens live in one module, `modules/users/`. Other
modules use only what its `public.py` exports.

## Protect an endpoint

```python
from {{ name.package }}.modules.users.public import CurrentUser


@router.get("/orders")
async def list_my_orders(user: CurrentUser, service: OrderServiceDep) -> OrderPage:
    return await service.list_for(user.id)
```

`CurrentUser` answers 401 without a valid `Authorization: Bearer <access
token>`, and hands the endpoint a `SignedInUser` (id, email, email_verified),
never the model. Keep `user.id` in your own tables; do not add a foreign key
into `users` from another module.

## The endpoints

They match the Flutter moarch's REST auth client, under `/api/v1/auth`:

| Endpoint | Body | Answers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST /register` | `{email, password}` | 201 `{access_token, refresh_token}` |
| `POST /login` | `{email, password}` | 200 tokens, 401 wrong email or password |
| `POST /logout` | `{refresh_token}` | 204 |
| `GET /me` | | `{id, email, name, email_verified}` |
| `DELETE /me` | | 204, the account and all it owns are deleted |
| `POST /device-token` | `{token}` | 204, the device can get pushes |

## Access tokens

HS256 JWTs signed with `JWT_SECRET`, valid `ACCESS_TOKEN_MINUTES` (15). The
app refuses to start outside `local` and `test` while the secret is the
placeholder or shorter than 32 characters. Generate one with
`python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"`.

## The password policy

`PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH` (8), `PASSWORD_MAX_LENGTH` (128), and
`PASSWORD_REQUIRE_UPPERCASE` / `_LOWERCASE` / `_NUMBER` / `_SYMBOL` (all
false). The defaults follow NIST SP 800-63B: length is what makes a password
strong; required character mixes push people to `Passw0rd!`. Passwords are
hashed with argon2id (pwdlib).

## Where to change it

`modules/users/parts.py` lists the optional parts (refresh tokens, lockout,
email verification). `dependencies.build_auth_parts` sets the ones this
project has; `moarch-py create auth` and `moarch-py create security lockout`
add theirs there.

